WEB SOURCE (the specification — read end to end)
  web/src/features/admin/components/devtools/tools/TimestampTool.tsx — a client-side developer utility (no
  network, no API hooks; the only hook is useTranslation). It:
    • Ticks a live `now` once a second (`setInterval(() => setNow(new Date()), 1000)`) and shows
      `Math.floor(now.getTime()/1000)` + `now.toISOString()` plus a "Now" button that fills both fields.
    • Converts a typed Unix epoch (`fromUnix`): empty ⇒ null; else `parseInt(unix,10)`, treating a raw string
      longer than 10 chars as milliseconds and otherwise as seconds (`*1000`); `new Date(ms)`; `isNaN` ⇒ null.
      Renders ISO / Local / Relative below the field when valid.
    • Converts a typed ISO 8601 string (`fromIso`): empty ⇒ null; else `new Date(iso)`; `isNaN` ⇒ null. Renders
      Unix / Local / Relative below the field when valid.
    • Composes `ToolCard` (a `GlassPanel` with a tinted icon + title + description) and `Input` / `Button` from
      `@/components/ui`; formats with `formatDateTime` (lib/dateFormat.ts → toLocaleString medium date + short
      time) and `getRelativeTime` (devtools/helpers.ts → Xs/Xm/Xh/Xd ago on the absolute, floored distance).
  i18n keys extracted from the source `t()` calls (ALL reproduced — the prompt's key list named only
  "Timestamp"; per the Honesty Covenant the source was read and every key reproduced, no scope narrowing):
    "Timestamp", "Timestamp Desc", "Now", "Unix Timestamp", "Iso", "Local", "Relative", "Iso Timestamp", "Unix".

