  font-mono text-cyan-300 values   → .monospaced() + Color.TS.accent, .textSelection(.enabled)
  now line "{unix} | {iso}"        → stacked Unix (body) + ISO (caption) rows (Apple-idiomatic; disclosed
                                     divergence from the inline `|` separator — same data, mobile-legible)
  fromUnix / fromIso (useMemo)     → TimestampParse.dateFromUnix / .dateFromISO (pure, unit-asserted)
  getRelativeTime / formatDateTime → TimestampFormat.relative / .localDateTime (ports, unit-asserted)
  i18n t(key)                      → TimestampStrings (NSLocalizedString table "TimestampTool"; web literal as the
                                     value: fallback so tests/preview bundles render deterministically)
  a11y                             → now row + each result line combined into single spoken elements; chip /
                                     refresh / "Now" / retry labelled; Dynamic Type via tokens; Reduce Motion via
                                     TSFadeIn / TSSkeleton
  telemetry                        → view.opened surface="TimestampTool" emitted once on start (P1/S11)

STATES (every one renders — no hidden surface)
  loading  → skeleton clock row + two field skeletons (the pre-first-tick moment; momentary in production).
  empty    → friendly ContentUnavailableView when the clock is unavailable, never a blank box.
  error    → retryable error chrome (P4 leaf addition; the web has no fetch to fail).
  data     → the live clock + the two converters; each converter shows its result lines only when the input
             parses (web's conditional `fromUnix && …` / `fromIso && …`), the field standing alone otherwise.
  stale    → header chip + banner + one-shot auto-refresh on the live→stale transition (a paused clock IS "data
             older than the freshness window").
  offline  → header chip + banner over the last-known time; no auto-refresh.

